        "notes": "Temperature of WASP-103 b from Kreidberg et al. (2018)'s map fitted to Hubble's 1.1 to 1.7 µm phase curve: the authors' own spherical-harmonic temperature map, as SPIDERMAN draws it from their released fit. It runs from 3,238 K at noon to 1,227 K at midnight, the extremes the paper prints. A phase curve sees longitudes, so the north-south shape comes from the harmonics, not the data. The false color runs from 0 to 3,900 K, the scale of the climate simulation, so the two can be compared. The shading is its star's light, a display convention: read the colors against the legend where the disc is lit."
